  "procedure": {
    "original_text": {
      "raw_value": "In an argon-filled glovebox, a threaded reaction tube (5 mL) equipped with a magnetic stir bar was charged with ethyl trifluoropyruvate (99 μL, 0.75 mmol, 1.5 equiv). A solution of freshly prepared allenyliron complex 1a (182 mg, 0.50 mmol, 1.0 equiv) in CH2Cl2 (0.5 mL) was then added, and the reaction tube was fitted with a septum cap and removed from the glovebox. The reaction mixture was then stirred at room temperature (24 °C) for 2.5 h. The crude mixture was concentrated in vacuo and purified by flash column chromatography on neutral aluminum oxide (hexanes/CH2Cl2 1/0 to 10/1 to 0/1) and subsequent recrystallization to provide the desired product 3 as a bright yellow solid. Yield: 128 mg, 48%.",
      "normalized_value": "In an argon-filled glovebox, a threaded reaction tube (5 mL) equipped with a magnetic stir bar was charged with ethyl trifluoropyruvate (99 μL, 0.75 mmol, 1.5 equiv). A solution of freshly prepared allenyliron complex 1a (182 mg, 0.50 mmol, 1.0 equiv) in CH2Cl2 (0.5 mL) was then added, and the reaction tube was fitted with a septum cap and removed from the glovebox. The reaction mixture was then stirred at room temperature (24 °C) for 2.5 h. The crude mixture was concentrated in vacuo and purified by flash column chromatography on neutral aluminum oxide (hexanes/CH2Cl2 1/0 to 10/1 to 0/1) and subsequent recrystallization to provide the desired product 3 as a bright yellow solid. Yield: 128 mg, 48%.",
      "acquisition_method": "original_extraction",
